From: pulpoff <pashkovsky@gmail.com>
Subject: The power button goes from the unlocked screen straight to the AOD (de.yesman.neo aod)

With aod on, blanking an unlocked screen made the lock screen and the AOD in the same go, and whichever drew
first showed: the lock screen flashed before the AOD (or, made after it, the lock screen covered it). A lock
screen made while the built-in panel is in AOD (power button, idle, lock delay, suspend) is now never seen:
it and its background stay transparent until the AOD goes away, and the AOD is stacked over it whichever was
made first. Waking shows the lock screen before the AOD goes, so unlocking still needs it. The AOD's style
provider is added once instead of once per AOD (each restyled the whole shell before the AOD's first frame).
---
--- a/src/aod.c	2026-11-02 00:51:19.733380376 +0100
+++ b/src/aod.c	2026-11-02 00:50:39.355852711 +0100
@@ -145,7 +145,7 @@
